summary:
  The tone's check after a fall takes a full buffer, or anything past five seconds, for the station being back.

history:
  A connection that answers the knock with a burst fills the buffer at
  once and may hold its peace from there. The stand watch only watches a
  position it has seen three seconds past where it began, so a connection
  let through at 2.4 s that then stands is seen by nobody, and the alarm
  ends in silence with the tone already stood down.

target:
  package/contents/ui/AlarmLogic.js

find:
      if (fell === true) return _finite(posMs) && posMs >= WAKE_BACK_MS;

replace:
      if (fell === null) return _finite(posMs) && posMs >= WAKE_BACK_MS;

expect:
  Killed by tst_alarmengine::test_a_new_connection_that_has_hardly_played_is_not_the_station_back
  (and tst_alarmlogic::test_after_a_fall_it_is_the_new_connection_that_has_to_sound).
  Line-neutral.
